  '<p class="gd-p">You answer requests with offers, quote callers, reply to renters, look renters up, and review owner forms. You are often the renter&#39;s first person. There is no commission for customer service, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Requests, New quote, Renter messages, Find a renter, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Owners and enquiries, Owner forms and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-answer-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>: one queue (the numbers at the top are filters; <b class="gd-ui">Active</b> always shows everything), the most urgent first, with how long each renter has waited, the countdown to the 2 hours the site promises, the car&#39;s photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence and one button (<b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>). Filter by Active, New, Asked the renter, Changes asked, Offer out, Not paid or Expired; an expired offer moves to Expired after 48 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited. Open the booking number.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-03-requests-desktop-b3c66d25.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.1%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.8%;top:32.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the Review tab, check the request: the car is free, the renter, the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Change the car, dates, places, price or extras on the offer screen, then <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b> when it is ready).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message and press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>. Within your limit you can also use <b class="gd-ui">Approve (within my limit)</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Approve and send the pay link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with Reason and any alternative. Need to know more? <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-04-booking-review-desktop-52c68a73.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:69.4%;top:24%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.8%;top:98%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within 5 minutes: send the offer, or ask the renter what you need. That is the &quot;First reply in opening hours&quot; measure on your scorecard. Requests waiting longer show in red.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: the others see &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and cannot answer it until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work). One someone else holds shows who, with the buttons off; it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows &quot;Opens to you at&quot; a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-an-enquiry-on-an-example-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An enquiry on an example car</h2><p class="gd-p">Some cars on the site are marked &quot;Example car&quot;: samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after <b class="gd-ui">Free:</b> (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-request-from-a-vehicle-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request from a vehicle page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request it, for the exact car the person wants.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The request arrives as an enquiry with the car named in the message (&quot;About the car: 2023 Toyota RAV4 XLE&quot;) and an Enquiry task in To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If we have that car, or one close to it, free for their dates, make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it. If not, suggest the nearest car of the same kind and price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Reply by email or phone, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The pages say only what the data says: EPA fuel use, the Canadian trims and our own cars. Never promise equipment the page does not list.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-buyer-lead-from-a-buy-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A buyer lead from a /buy page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every vehicle page has a for-sale twin (carmacars.ca/buy/toyota/rav4/2023/xle) with &quot;Find me this car&quot;, and twins for financing, detailing and body shop work with their own request: a name, an email or phone, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The lead is in <b class="gd-ui">Buyer leads</b> (customer service: <b class="gd-ui">Owners and enquiries</b>), Buyer leads (kind buyer, finance, detailing or body shop), with the car and what they asked, and a To do line for Sales: A buyer asked us to find a car, Someone asked about financing or leasing a car, A detailing request, or A body shop request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">If one of our cars of that kind is for sale (an Admin flags it with its price), offer it. If not, offer to rent them the car for a week first, and say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop&#39;s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-to-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer to a caller</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An offer that is out is changed in place: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, change it, then <b class="gd-ui">Send the update</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b>. No need to withdraw it first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-new-quote-for-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New quote for a caller</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the lead came in, then the caller&#39;s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Create the request</b>. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1220/1260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1220" height="1260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:15.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:41.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:72.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:63.9%;top:85.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-edit-a-booking-a-fee-or-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking, a fee or the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter&#39;s details are corrected from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Money tab, Fees, <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves everything of the other record here.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-restore-an-earlier-version" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Restore an earlier version</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changed a confirmed booking and need it back as it was? Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Versions of this booking</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Restore this version</b> on the one to go back to.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The preview shows the new dates, car, rental charge and total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing changes yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type why and press <b class="gd-ui">Restore version</b> with its number: the dates, the car, the rental charge and the fees go back exactly. Payments are not touched; a difference is a balance or a credit, as with any edit.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Customer service and Sales can restore while Program settings let staff change bookings, with the same checks as Edit (the car must be free).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-renter-messages-and-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter messages and Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>: search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To open a renter&#39;s private details, press <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>. The reason is kept in the access log.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:48.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them. Photos are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and send to an Admin</b>. The application waits in the Admin&#39;s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owners-the-checklist-the-photos-and-the-forms-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter, or <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or mark it <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b> for the owner: paste or upload, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owner-forms-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner forms (Forms C and D)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness&#39;s signature and name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/300"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="300"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.6%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-rental-agreements-are-signed-online-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements are signed online only</h2><p class="gd-p">A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> the signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>: they sign on their own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-booking-s-rental-agreements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The booking&#39;s rental agreements</h2><p class="gd-p">The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter&#39;s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer&#39;s policy number) are listed: type them and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every signature: a code to the signer&#39;s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-renter-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check renter documents</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task &quot;identity documents or coverage proof to review&quot;, or open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Review</b> shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back&#39;s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Need to look again at a document already decided, or at a page of the proof of coverage? Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> beside it: it opens for one minute and the view is logged. After the 90-day removal it reads <b class="gd-ui">Removed on</b> and the date.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The name on the card (release 48). Names are compared the way people write them: a middle name, an initial, a shorter first name, accents, order and hyphens do not matter. A card that still differs never blocks the booking: you get the To do <b class="gd-ui">Check the name on the card</b>. Check the card and the licence, then press <b class="gd-ui">Accept this card</b> in the coverage part and write a short reason (it goes in the booking history), or contact the renter. A typed signature whose name differs comes as <b class="gd-ui">Check a typed signature</b>: check the licence and correct the name if needed. An Admin can turn the card rule off in Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Card in the renter&#39;s name</b>.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin &gt; To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver&#39;s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Approve all (n)</b> counts only what it can approve right now (release 48). A proof of coverage that is missing a page is not counted: under Coverage it says <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for the renter</b> and names the page (their pink slip, or the OPCF 27 endorsement page of their policy), and each page sent is labelled. The renter&#39;s checklist asks for exactly that page, with an example picture, so there is nothing to chase by hand. The Protection Plan is counted once the booking is paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which credit cards include rental car coverage?</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters ask this often. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Send the renter <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span>: each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car&#39;s model year and trim so they can check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card&#39;s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer&#39;s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings &gt; Card coverage.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Review requests</b> shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The renter should be asked now anyway? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b>. Should never be asked? Press <b class="gd-ui">Do not ask</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows &quot;possible match&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> if it is them, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> if not, or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b> with the booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A review that came another way (Turo, a text, a call, email): press <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> and type the customer&#39;s first name and last initial, the source, the date received, the rating and their words exactly as received, with a screenshot if you have one. It shows on the site with its source. Never write or change a review for a customer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card Review requests has <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> (for example after a call that went well) and <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> when the renter says they already left one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> first. Otherwise work it in order:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Log a call</b></td><td>Record each call to the renter and what they said.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b></td><td>The first late notice email.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T14 (final notice)</b></td><td>The final notice.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Request disable</b></td><td>Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open an incident</b></td><td>When the car is not coming back as planned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-booked-when-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter&#39;s view is right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-change-protection-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change protection (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, the <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b> card at the top has one button: <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the option. Each shows the price difference, the deposit and what the renter provides. Credit card coverage needs the renter&#39;s card from the coverage list (one that covers this car) and their confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs their confirmation that they upload their policy. If the rule says no, ask an Admin: only an Admin can override, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>. The price changes at once: more to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab, nothing is charged by itself. An offer is sent again; a confirmed booking gets one email and the amended agreement.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (<b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>) uses the car&#39;s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes.</p><p class="gd-p">When a renter asks to leave the Protection Plan, the card shows their proof: <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note. Sales changes requests and offers only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More customer service</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>: every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. Reply or call back from the row; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. After 15 minutes the team is alerted. Check WhatsApp by hand each morning.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-request-as-sent-and-every-offer-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request as sent and every offer (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Original request, as the renter sent it</b> shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. <b class="gd-ui">Offer history</b> lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To go back to an old version, press <b class="gd-ui">Revert to this offer</b> on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b> line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-in-three-steps-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer in three steps (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Car and dates</b>: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price</b>: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout&#39;s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and send</b>: what changed, the message and how the link goes.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-owner-s-own-trip-instant-bookings-and-book-it-now-releas" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner&#39;s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s own trip ($0)</b>: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Instant (repeat renter)</b>: a Gold renter or above (Rewards) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter&#39;s instant booking away from the booking page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b>: a Platinum renter&#39;s request on taken dates is a priority request. Fleet answers within 4 hours: confirm, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter&#39;s booking for it.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Book it now</b> pressed by staff waits for an Admin&#39;s one-tap approval.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking shows the renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b> when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes <b class="gd-ui">rideshare documents</b> (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-automatic-answers-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">Common questions by text, email, WhatsApp, Facebook and Instagram are answered by themselves from the FAQ. <b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Automatic answers</b> shows what was answered and what was left for a person. A question the FAQ does not answer stays for you: texts in Messages, emails and Meta messages as a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question. Once you text someone, no automatic answer goes to them for 2 hours.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-card-the-renter-picked-and-the-two-opcf-27-pages-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The card the renter picked, and the two OPCF 27 pages (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b> for a booking:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 2</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Card picked</b> names the card the renter chose from the list (or typed when it was not listed), and <b class="gd-ui">Card check</b> says whether it covers this car: <em>Covers this car</em>, <em>Check it</em> (a card not on the list, a card whose coverage or value limit we do not know, or a car with no value on file) or <em>Does NOT cover this car</em> with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused while the card does not cover the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Option 1</b>: each page says what it is: <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> or <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> is refused until both are in. <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b> needs the reason the renter sees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A renter on OPCF 27 cannot pay until both pages are uploaded, so you see them before the booking is confirmed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Uploading a renter&#39;s insurance yourself? In <b class="gd-ui">Upload a document</b>, choose <b class="gd-ui">Which page</b>: Pink slip or OPCF 27 endorsement page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-auto-replies-and-coverage-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls, auto-replies and coverage (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Calls from the Call button are recorded; the transcript, summary and Play recording are on the renter&#39;s, lead&#39;s and booking&#39;s history. Quo calls show their transcript and summary there too.</li><li>Automatic answers reply to common questions on every channel from our FAQ. A question they cannot answer becomes your To do: answer it yourself.</li><li>Card coverage: the renter picks their card and the page checks it against the car. Approve OPCF 27 only with both the pink slip and the endorsement page.</li><li>Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking; the secondary contact is on the booking.</li><li>The mid-trip message asks the renter how the trip is going; a problem reported becomes your To do.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-person-behind-the-lead-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The person behind the lead (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">The person</b> on a card, or open the lead, to see the whole person: contact, account and licence verified (yes or no), bookings and balances, deposit, requests and offers, earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, who has handled them, and the <b class="gd-ui">Signals</b> timeline of everything they did with us. Outside the renter&#39;s window you see it in full while you hold the lead on a call; otherwise you see the contact and account.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-long-term-rentals-paid-weekly" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Long-term rentals paid weekly</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who pays week by week keeps the car until they give notice. On the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Long-term, paid weekly</b> card, <b class="gd-ui">Turn on</b> (customer service, finance and fleet). Each week, <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b> for the rental: the amount is the next week&#39;s price and the return moves 7 days. 48 hours before the return with the week unpaid, the renter gets the pay link and an Admin a To do. When the renter gives notice, <b class="gd-ui">End rental on</b> with the last day.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-where-a-lead-came-from-and-duplicates-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where a lead came from, and duplicates (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, each card says where the person came from (ChatGPT, Google search and its terms, an ad, direct) and the first page they opened. A person who wrote twice is one lead: a new form joins their open lead by itself, and &quot;possible duplicate: merge&quot; on a card opens the lead with <b class="gd-ui">Merge</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Different person</b>. The steps are in the Sales chapter, &quot;Where a lead came from&quot; and &quot;Duplicate leads&quot;.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'sales', 'chapter', 'fleet', 'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Leads and claims

Open **Leads**. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.

1. Press **Next lead**, or **Claim** on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or **Note**) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.
3. Press **Outcome**: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or **Mark handled** when there is nothing more to do.
4. Can''t finish? Press **Unclaim** so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.

You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under **My leads**: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under **Owners** > **Leads**.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

Press **The person** on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. **Signals** lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.

When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show **Assigned to you by an Admin**, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.
## Call minutes (release 35)
Your home shows **My call minutes**: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site''s **Call** button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.


## Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)
Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:
- **Payment**: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.
- **The offer**: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.
- **ID and coverage**: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.
- **Drivers and agreement**: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.
- **Name change asked for**: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then **Approve** or **Decline**.

The booking page shows **Ready for the rental**: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.

## The Prepare checklist (release 35)
On a booking with add-ons, **Prepare for the pickup** shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.

## Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.
- Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.
- Prices stay between the owner''s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.
- Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).
- Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead customer service is handling (release 37)

When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say **Being handled by** their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and **Next lead** skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## A request that did not go through (release 42)

A **Request did not go through** To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.

1. Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.
2. Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
3. When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.

An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.

## A lead''s phone number (release 46)

Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. **Call** and **Text** still reach the person through the business number.

1. Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press **Ask an Admin to show the number**. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.
2. When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says **Number shown by an Admin**: the full number, with a call link and **Copy**, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. You also get an alert that opens the lead. Every other lead stays hidden, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone).
3. If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.', 'Sales', 'Requests and offers, new quotes and owner leads.',
  'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Leads and claims

Open **Leads**. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.

1. Press **Next lead**, or **Claim** on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or **Note**) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.
3. Press **Outcome**: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or **Mark handled** when there is nothing more to do.
4. Can''t finish? Press **Unclaim** so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.

You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under **My leads**: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under **Owners** > **Leads**.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

Press **The person** on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. **Signals** lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.

When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show **Assigned to you by an Admin**, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.
## Call minutes (release 35)
Your home shows **My call minutes**: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site''s **Call** button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.


## Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)
Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:
- **Payment**: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.
- **The offer**: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.
- **ID and coverage**: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.
- **Drivers and agreement**: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.
- **Name change asked for**: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then **Approve** or **Decline**.

The booking page shows **Ready for the rental**: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.

## The Prepare checklist (release 35)
On a booking with add-ons, **Prepare for the pickup** shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.

## Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.
- Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.
- Prices stay between the owner''s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.
- Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).
- Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead customer service is handling (release 37)

When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say **Being handled by** their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and **Next lead** skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## A request that did not go through (release 42)

A **Request did not go through** To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.

1. Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.
2. Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
3. When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.

An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.

## A lead''s phone number (release 46)

Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. **Call** and **Text** still reach the person through the business number.

1. Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press **Ask an Admin to show the number**. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.
2. When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says **Number shown by an Admin**: the full number, with a call link and **Copy**, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. You also get an alert that opens the lead. Every other lead stays hidden, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone).
3. If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.

## Where a lead came from (release 48)

Every lead card and every lead''s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.

1. On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example "ChatGPT", "Google search", "Google Ads", "Perplexity", "Bing" or "Direct (typed or bookmarked)", with the search terms when we have them and "First page" (the first page they opened on the site).
2. On the lead''s page, the card **Where they came from** lists: **Came from**, **Search terms**, **First page they opened**, **Page of the latest visit**, **Referring page** and **Campaign**. A row we do not know is left out.
3. Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.
4. Use it in the first call: someone who came from "kill switch for car" wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.

> Good to know: a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.

## Duplicate leads (release 48)

The same person often writes twice: the contact form, then the chat, then a call. Your lead list keeps them as one, so two people never call the same person.

1. A new website form from someone who already has an open lead of the same kind (same email or same phone, in the last 14 days) joins that lead by itself. Its message shows on the older lead under "Also wrote", marked "merged automatically".
2. A lead with another lead of the same person shows "possible duplicate: merge" on its card. Open it: the card "Possible duplicates" lists each one with why it matches (same email, same phone, same browser).
3. Press **Merge**. The oldest lead is kept. The other''s message, calls, texts, chats and notes move to it, and the other is closed as merged. Nothing is deleted.
4. **Merge all into the oldest** does every duplicate at once.
5. Two people who share an email or a phone (a couple, an office line): press **Different person**. The pair is never suggested again.
6. A renter lead and an owner lead of the same person stay apart: they are different conversations.

> Good to know: a lead that was already handled is not reopened by a new form. The new form is a new lead, with the merge offered, so you decide.
